</ul>
<p><img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/ab571f/7589297383/il_794xN.7589297383_lr1w.jpg" alt="Hexagon Display Shelves"></p>
<p>While designed with Smiski in mind, these also work for Sonny Angel, Hippers, blind box collections, mini figures, and dollhouse accessories.</p>
<h2 id="more-than-display-shelves">More Than Display Shelves</h2>
<p>Infinite Builds also creates dollhouse furniture &#x26; miniatures, DIY miniature kits, custom 3D printed displays, and bulk 3D printing for shops, creators, and businesses.</p>
<h2 id="build-your-tiny-world">Build Your Tiny World</h2>
<p>Collecting doesn’t stop after opening the blind box — that’s where the fun begins. Give your Smiski a home, build them a neighborhood, create a tiny world that makes you smile every time you walk by.</p>
<p><img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/282407/7955030717/il_794xN.7955030717_ia7z.jpg" alt="Build Your Tiny World"></p> ','https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0962/4138/5545/articles/il_fullxfull.8035441896_ef5y.webp?v=1783054983','Minh Hoang','2026-07-03','published',NULL,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug,title,excerpt,content,cover,author,published_at,status,seo_description,og_image) VALUES ('3-trending-display-ideas-for-smiski-sonny-angel-in-2026','3 Trending Display Ideas for Smiski & Sonny Angel in 2026','How to Style Your Mini Figures for Aesthetic & Collectible Setups',' <h2 id="how-to-style-your-mini-figures-for-aesthetic--collectible-setups">How to Style Your Mini Figures for Aesthetic &#x26; Collectible Setups</h2>
<p>Smiski and Sonny Angel have become a key part of modern desk decor and aesthetic room setups. In 2026, the trend is shifting from simply collecting figures to how they are displayed.</p>
<h2 id="-1-mini-shelf-display--structured--playful-layout">🌿 1. Mini Shelf Display – Structured &#x26; Playful Layout</h2>
<p>Multiple levels, steps, and platforms create natural variation in height and positioning. Creates depth through multiple display levels, highlights each figure individually, maintains a clean and organized look.</p>
<p><img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/0c3e94/7572323324/il_794xN.7572323324_vazc.jpg" alt="1. Mini Shelf Display">
<img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/b200be/6930621551/il_794xN.6930621551_ieit.jpg" alt="1. Mini Shelf Display"></p>
<h2 id="-2-honeycomb-wall-display--clean--modern-aesthetic">🧩 2. Honeycomb Wall Display – Clean &#x26; Modern Aesthetic</h2>
<p>Hexagon-shaped shelves create a geometric arrangement that is clean and visually striking, maximizing wall space while maintaining a minimal layout — popular among those who prefer a structured visual style.</p>
<p><img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/484133/7541356878/il_794xN.7541356878_s6r6.jpg" alt="2. Honeycomb Wall Display">
<img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/08d359/7589296141/il_794xN.7589296141_kdle.jpg" alt="2. Honeycomb Wall Display">
<img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/e8473d/7541356866/il_794xN.7541356866_4py9.jpg" alt="2. Honeycomb Wall Display">
<img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/ab571f/7589297383/il_794xN.7589297383_lr1w.jpg" alt="2. Honeycomb Wall Display"></p>
<h2 id="-3-planter-display--turning-figures-into-living-decor">🪴 3. Planter Display – Turning Figures into Living Decor</h2>
<p>Placing figures inside or around mini planters blends collectible toys with natural elements, creating a soft, organic aesthetic — unique presentation, compatible with desk setups, strong appeal for gifting and lifestyle photography.</p>
<p><img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/f627ed/7620256027/il_794xN.7620256027_ibbb.jpg" alt="3. Planter Display">
<img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/1f91b9/7525019170/il_794xN.7525019170_9qvj.jpg" alt="3. Planter Display"></p>
<h2 id="-why-display-matters-more-than-ever">🌟 Why Display Matters More Than Ever</h2>
<p>A well-designed display enhances the perceived value of each piece, creates a cohesive aesthetic, and makes the collection more engaging and personal.</p>
<h2 id="-final-thoughts">✨ Final Thoughts</h2>
<p>Smiski and Sonny Angel displays have evolved into a form of personal expression — whether through miniature scenes, structured wall layouts, or creative planter setups, each style offers a unique way to showcase your collection.</p> ','https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0962/4138/5545/articles/Set_164_1_1.png?v=1774846792','Minh Hoang','2026-03-30','published',NULL,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug,title,excerpt,content,cover,author,published_at,status,seo_description,og_image) VALUES ('best-mini-planters-for-desk-aesthetic','Best Mini Planters for Desk Aesthetic','🌿 Small Details That Make a Big Difference',' <h2 id="-small-details-that-make-a-big-difference">🌿 Small Details That Make a Big Difference</h2>
<p>A clean, aesthetic desk setup isn’t just about your monitor or keyboard — it’s the small details that bring everything together. Mini planters add life, texture, and personality without taking up too much space.</p>
<p><img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/439e56/7613862669/il_794xN.7613862669_i8qb.jpg" alt="1. Minimal Cylinder Planter">
<img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/d2d0f2/7613803477/il_794xN.7613803477_1pqd.jpg" alt="2. Square Planter">
<img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/5116a9/7613849875/il_794xN.7613849875_h421.jpg" alt="3. Organic / Wavy Planter">
<img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/30f1b7/7565905412/il_794xN.7565905412_bgfv.jpg" alt="3. Organic / Wavy Planter">
<img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/8eebdb/7599495393/il_794xN.7599495393_l4w6.jpg" alt="4. Unique Shape Planter">
<img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/0d2ca6/7565826230/il_794xN.7565826230_ooht.jpg" alt="4. Unique Shape Planter">
<img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/94ff53/7565930752/il_794xN.7565930752_t3l1.jpg" alt="5. Terracotta Style Planter"></p>
<h2 id="-why-mini-planters-work-so-well">🌱 Why Mini Planters Work So Well</h2>
<p>They add a natural, calming element, fit perfectly in small spaces, match minimalist and aesthetic setups, and work with both real and artificial plants.</p>
<h2 id="planter-styles">Planter Styles</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>🪴 Minimal Cylinder Planter</strong> — smooth shape, clean look; place near keyboard/mouse, combine 2–3 for symmetry.</li>
<li><strong>🧱 Square Planter</strong> — sharp edges, modern feel; corner of desk or next to monitor stand.</li>
<li><strong>🍃 Organic / Wavy Planter</strong> — adds personality, more playful; centerpiece of desk, combine with simpler pots.</li>
<li><strong>🎃 Unique Shape Planter</strong> — eye-catching statement piece; use only 1, pair with neutral decor.</li>
<li><strong>🏺 Terracotta Style Planter</strong> — warm tone, cozy feeling; combine with wood desk, pair with green plants.</li>
</ul>
<h2 id="-how-to-choose-the-right-mini-planter">🎯 How to Choose the Right Mini Planter</h2>
<p>Consider your desk style (minimal/cute/natural), how much space you have (1–2 for small desks, 3–5 for large), and whether you want focus (1 standout) or balance (2–3 types).</p>
<h2 id="️-common-mistakes">⚠️ Common Mistakes</h2>
<p>Using too many planters, mixing too many styles, choosing pots too large for the desk. Rule: keep it simple.</p>
<h2 id="-suggested-setup">🛍 Suggested Setup</h2>
<p>1 cylinder planter + 1 square planter + 1 wavy planter — gives balance, texture, and aesthetic variety.</p>
<h2 id="-final-thoughts">🌟 Final Thoughts</h2>
<p>Mini planters are small, but they completely change how your desk feels.</p> ','https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0962/4138/5545/articles/il_fullxfull.7613862667_opm4.webp?v=1774845992','Minh Hoang','2026-03-30','published',NULL,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug,title,excerpt,content,cover,author,published_at,status,seo_description,og_image) VALUES ('cute-desk-setup-ideas-with-miniature-decor','Cute Desk Setup Ideas with Miniature Decor','🌿 Transform Your Workspace into a Cozy Mini World',' <h2 id="-transform-your-workspace-into-a-cozy-mini-world">🌿 Transform Your Workspace into a Cozy Mini World</h2>
<p>A cute desk setup is more than just aesthetics — it creates a space that feels personal, inspiring, and enjoyable to work in. Miniature decor is one of the easiest ways to elevate your desk without taking up too much space.</p>
<h2 id="-1-start-with-a-soft-minimal-base">✨ 1. Start with a Soft Minimal Base</h2>
<p>Neutral desk (white, beige, wood), soft lighting (natural sunlight works best), minimal clutter — helps your miniature pieces stand out more.</p>
<h2 id="-2-add-mini-planters-for-a-fresh-look">🪴 2. Add Mini Planters for a Fresh Look</h2>
<p>Place 1–3 mini plants near your keyboard, mix shapes (round, square, textured), use soft green tones for a calming effect.</p>
<p><img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/0d2ca6/7565826230/il_794xN.7565826230_ooht.jpg" alt="2. Add Mini Planters">
<img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/50bb53/7613757313/il_794xN.7613757313_ltce.jpg" alt="2. Add Mini Planters"></p>
<h2 id="-3-use-miniature-furniture-as-decor-accents">🪑 3. Use Miniature Furniture as Decor Accents</h2>
<p>A tiny chair beside your monitor, a mini bench under a shelf, a small bookshelf near your mousepad act as visual anchors.</p>
<h2 id="-4-add-cute-characters-or-figures">🧸 4. Add Cute Characters or Figures</h2>
<p>Keep it to 1–3 figures (avoid clutter), match color palette (pastel/neutral), combine with mini furniture for storytelling.</p>
<h2 id="-5-create-a-mini-scene-signature-look">🏠 5. Create a Mini Scene (Signature Look)</h2>
<p>Using a room box + furniture + accessories, create a full miniature story — a tiny kitchen corner, a reading nook, a mini café scene.</p>
<p><img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/b200be/6930621551/il_794xN.6930621551_ieit.jpg" alt="5. Create a Mini Scene">
<img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/322a96/7589949244/il_794xN.7589949244_t0j5.jpg" alt="5. Create a Mini Scene"></p>
<h2 id="-6-stick-to-a-color-theme">🎨 6. Stick to a Color Theme</h2>
<p>Popular themes: pastel (pink, yellow, mint), minimal (white, beige), natural (wood + green), cute/kawaii mix.</p>
<h2 id="-7-keep-it-balanced-important">💡 7. Keep It Balanced (Important)</h2>
<p>Rule: 70% functional space, 30% decor. Miniatures should enhance your workspace, not distract from it.</p>
<h2 id="-final-thoughts">🌟 Final Thoughts</h2>
<p>A cute desk setup doesn’t require big changes — just small, thoughtful details. With the right pieces, your desk can feel like a tiny world of your own.</p> ','https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0962/4138/5545/articles/Set_164.png?v=1774843632','Minh Hoang','2026-03-28','published',NULL,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug,title,excerpt,content,cover,author,published_at,status,seo_description,og_image) VALUES ('from-idea-to-product-our-miniature-workflow','From Idea to Product: Our Miniature Workflow','How Infinite Builds Turns Concepts into Real Miniatures',' <h2 id="how-infinite-builds-turns-concepts-into-real-miniatures">How Infinite Builds Turns Concepts into Real Miniatures</h2>
<p>Creating a miniature product is more than just 3D printing — it’s a full process of design, testing, refining, and storytelling.</p>
<h2 id="-1-it-starts-with-an-idea">💡 1. It Starts with an Idea</h2>
<p>Focus on everyday objects (chairs, kitchen sets, planters), aesthetic decor (soft shapes, minimal style), and functional miniature pieces — something small but meaningful and visually satisfying.</p>
<h2 id="-2-designing-in-3d-cad-stage">🎨 2. Designing in 3D (CAD Stage)</h2>
<p>Using CAD software (like Fusion 360): correct scale (usually 1:12), smooth soft shapes, print-friendly geometry, proper thickness to avoid breaking.</p>
<p><img src="https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0962/4138/5545/files/z7672358674034_1cd1e9c4b24af7d182315683a0644a09.jpg?v=1774845212&#x26;width=900" alt="2. Designing in 3D"></p>
<h2 id="-3-first-prototype-3d-printing">🖨 3. First Prototype (3D Printing)</h2>
<p>Testing proportions in real life, surface quality, stability, and assembly. A design that looks perfect on screen can feel “off” in real life — most adjustments happen here.</p>
<p><img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/785d8d/7624823636/il_794xN.7624823636_knb6.jpg" alt="3. First Prototype"></p>
<h2 id="-4-refinement--iteration">🔧 4. Refinement &#x26; Iteration</h2>
<p>Adjust dimensions, improve curves, fix weak points, re-print multiple versions until the product looks right, feels right, and prints consistently.</p>
<h2 id="-5-final-product--styling">🌟 5. Final Product &#x26; Styling</h2>
<p>Clean, minimal setups, soft lighting (natural shadows), real-life context (desk/dollhouse) — helps customers visualize how the product fits into their space.</p>
<p><img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/18dc97/7672771915/il_794xN.7672771915_sw77.jpg" alt="5. Final Product"></p>
<h2 id="-6-from-workshop-to-customer">📦 6. From Workshop to Customer</h2>
<p>Printed in small batches, checked for quality manually, packed carefully.</p>
<h2 id="-what-makes-our-workflow-different">🧠 What Makes Our Workflow Different?</h2>
<p>Infinite Builds designs everything in-house, tests every product physically, focuses on both aesthetic and usability, and builds for real miniature lovers.</p>
<h2 id="-final-thoughts">🌿 Final Thoughts</h2>
<p>From idea → CAD → prototype → final product, every step is intentional.</p> ','https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0962/4138/5545/articles/il_fullxfull.7624823656_qvzo.webp?v=1774845353','Minh Hoang','2026-03-28','published',NULL,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug,title,excerpt,content,cover,author,published_at,status,seo_description,og_image) VALUES ('the-complete-guide-to-3d-printing-miniatures','The Complete Guide to 3D Printing Miniatures','A Practical Maker''s Guide by Infinite Builds',' <h2 id="a-practical-makers-guide-by-infinite-builds">A Practical Maker’s Guide by Infinite Builds</h2>
<p>3D printing miniatures has transformed how makers design, prototype, and produce small-scale models. At Infinite Builds, we design and print miniatures daily using CAD software and multiple desktop 3D printers.</p>
<h2 id="1-what-counts-as-a-3d-printed-miniature">1. What Counts as a 3D Printed Miniature?</h2>
<p>Small-scale models (1:6, 1:12, 1:24, 1:64, etc.), printed using FDM or resin printers, designed digitally in CAD software, used for dollhouses, dioramas, display scenes, or collectibles.</p>
<h2 id="2-choosing-the-right-printing-technology">2. Choosing the Right Printing Technology</h2>
<p><strong>FDM (Filament Printing)</strong> — best for furniture, structural pieces, DIY kits, large miniatures. Pros: strong parts, affordable materials, easier post-processing. Limitations: visible layer lines, less fine detail than resin.</p>
<p><strong>Resin Printing (SLA/MSLA)</strong> — best for tiny props, figurines, decorative food items, high-detail parts. Pros: extremely fine detail, smooth surface. Limitations: more post-processing, resin handling safety required.</p>
<h2 id="3-understanding-scale-in-miniatures">3. Understanding Scale in Miniatures</h2>
<p>1:12 scale (dollhouse standard), 1:24 scale (half scale), 1:64 scale (small diorama/vehicle scenes). Always convert real-world dimensions to scale, use consistent units (mm recommended), double-check wall thickness.</p>
<p>Example: a real chair 90cm tall → 7.5cm at 1:12, 3.75cm at 1:24.</p>
<h2 id="4-recommended-print-settings-for-miniatures-fdm">4. Recommended Print Settings for Miniatures (FDM)</h2>
<p>Layer height: 0.08–0.16mm. Nozzle size: 0.2mm or 0.4mm. Print speed: slower for better detail. Infill: 10–20% for small pieces. Cooling: high for sharp details.</p>
<h2 id="5-design-tips-for-better-miniature-prints">5. Design Tips for Better Miniature Prints</h2>
<ol>
<li>Avoid ultra-thin walls (min 1–1.2mm for FDM)</li>
<li>Add chamfers &#x26; fillets (hard 90° corners print less cleanly)</li>
<li>Orient smartly (surface quality depends on print orientation)</li>
<li>Separate tiny parts (small decorative elements print cleaner separately)</li>
</ol>
<h2 id="6-post-processing-for-professional-results">6. Post-Processing for Professional Results</h2>
<p>Sand lightly (400–800 grit), use primer before painting, apply acrylic paint for details, use matte sealant. For resin: wash in IPA, cure under UV light, sand gently if needed.</p>
<h2 id="7-common-mistakes-beginners-make">7. Common Mistakes Beginners Make</h2>
<p>Printing too fast, using thick layer height, ignoring scale consistency, designing parts too thin, over-supporting delicate parts.</p>
<h2 id="8-how-3d-printing-supports-miniature-businesses">8. How 3D Printing Supports Miniature Businesses</h2>
<p>Rapid prototyping, small batch production, customization options, low inventory risk — helps design, test, and refine models before launching as DIY kits or finished miniatures.</p>
<h2 id="9-final-thoughts">9. Final Thoughts</h2>
<p>Key factors influencing quality: correct scale conversion, appropriate printer type, fine-tuned settings, careful post-processing.</p> ','https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0962/4138/5545/articles/il_1588xN.7572323324_vazc.webp?v=1774844303','Minh Hoang','2026-03-28','published',NULL,NULL);
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO posts (slug,title,excerpt,content,cover,author,published_at,status,seo_description,og_image) VALUES ('understanding-miniature-scale-1-12-vs-1-24-vs-1-64','Understanding Miniature Scale (1:12 vs 1:24 vs 1:64)','Complete Beginner Guide for Miniature & Dollhouse Builders',' <h2 id="complete-beginner-guide-for-miniature--dollhouse-builders">Complete Beginner Guide for Miniature &#x26; Dollhouse Builders</h2>
<p>Choosing the wrong scale can lead to mismatched furniture, unrealistic scenes, or products that simply don’t fit together.</p>
<h2 id="-what-does-scale-mean">📏 What Does “Scale” Mean?</h2>
<p>Scale represents the ratio between a real object and its miniature version. Example: at 1:12 scale, a 120cm table becomes 10cm.</p>
<h2 id="-112-scale--the-most-popular-dollhouse-scale">🏠 1:12 Scale – The Most Popular Dollhouse Scale</h2>
<p>Most common scale in dollhouse world, high detail, realistic look. Chair ~7–10cm, table ~10–12cm. Best for dollhouse setups, room box displays, detailed miniature furniture, beginners.</p>
<p><img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/e19a2e/7613785552/il_794xN.7613785552_a8ye.jpg" alt="1:12 Scale">
<img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/17c87c/7624732150/il_794xN.7624732150_lixs.jpg" alt="1:12 Scale"></p>
<h2 id="-124-scale--smaller-more-compact">🧩 1:24 Scale – Smaller, More Compact</h2>
<p>Half the size of 1:12, takes less space, slightly less detail. Chair ~3–5cm, table ~5–6cm. Best for small desk displays, compact dioramas, travel-friendly setups.</p>
<h2 id="-164-scale--tiny--collectible">🚗 1:64 Scale – Tiny &#x26; Collectible</h2>
<p>Very small scale, often used with model cars, focus on overall scene rather than detail. Chair ~1–2cm, table ~2–3cm. Best for dioramas, street scenes, collectors.</p>
<p><img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/b1f85e/6420268525/il_794xN.6420268525_83av.jpg" alt="1:64 Scale">
<img src="https://i.etsystatic.com/49165183/r/il/08eb2f/6420186099/il_794xN.6420186099_48ts.jpg" alt="1:64 Scale"></p>
<h2 id="️-quick-comparison">⚖️ Quick Comparison</h2>





























<table><thead><tr><th>Scale</th><th>Size</th><th>Detail</th><th>Best Use</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1:12</td><td>Large</td><td>⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐</td><td>Dollhouse, beginners</td></tr><tr><td>1:24</td><td>Medium</td><td>⭐⭐⭐</td><td>Compact displays</td></tr><tr><td>1:64</td><td>Small</td><td>⭐⭐</td><td>Dioramas, collectibles</td></tr></tbody></table>
<h2 id="-common-mistakes-to-avoid">❌ Common Mistakes to Avoid</h2>
<p>Mixing different scales in one scene, buying furniture without checking scale, designing too thin for small scales, ignoring proportion consistency.</p>
<h2 id="-how-to-choose-the-right-scale">💡 How to Choose the Right Scale</h2>
<p>Consider space (large desk → 1:12, small space → 1:24/1:64), goal (realistic room → 1:12, cute decor → 1:24, diorama → 1:64), and whether buying (follow product scale) or building (choose scale first).</p>
<h2 id="-suggested-scale-for-beginners">🛍 Suggested Scale for Beginners</h2>
<p>Go with 1:12 scale — easier to handle, more products available, better detail, less frustrating.</p>
<h2 id="-final-thoughts">🌟 Final Thoughts</h2>
<p>Understanding scale is the foundation of building beautiful miniatures.</p> ','https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0962/4138/5545/articles/il_1588xN.7589430837_8frf.webp?v=1774844119','Minh Hoang','2026-03-28','published',NULL,NULL);
